{"id":"mahabharata-7-134","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":134,"title":"चतुस्त्रिंशदधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 134 · Ashvatthaman and Karna's quarrel","summary":{"en":"Ashvatthaman, enraged at Karna's insult to his uncle Kripa, raises his sword to kill him, and Duryodhana and Kripa pacify them. Ashvatthaman then vows to fight Arjuna himself, and the battle goes on with great slaughter.","kn":"ತನ್ನ ಸೋದರಮಾವ ಕೃಪನಿಗೆ ಕರ್ಣ ಮಾಡಿದ ಅವಮಾನದಿಂದ ಕೆರಳಿದ ಅಶ್ವತ್ಥಾಮ ಖಡ್ಗ ಎತ್ತಿ ಅವನನ್ನು ಕೊಲ್ಲಲು ಹೋಗುತ್ತಾನೆ; ದುರ್ಯೋಧನ, ಕೃಪರು ಶಮನ ಮಾಡುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಅಶ್ವತ್ಥಾಮ ತಾನೇ ಅರ್ಜುನನೊಡನೆ ಹೋರಾಡುವೆನೆನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಭೀಕರ ಸಂಹಾರ ಮುಂದುವರಿಯುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"कर्ण द्वारा अपने मामा कृप के अपमान पर क्रुद्ध अश्वत्थामा तलवार उठाकर उसे मारने को बढ़ता है, और दुर्योधन तथा कृप उन्हें शान्त करते हैं। अश्वत्थामा स्वयं अर्जुन से लड़ने की प्रतिज्ञा करता है और भीषण संहार चलता है।","te":"తన మేనమామ కృపుని కర్ణుడు అవమానించడంతో కోపించిన అశ్వత్థామ ఖడ్గం ఎత్తి అతన్ని చంపబోతాడు; దుర్యోధనుడు, కృపుడు శాంతింపజేస్తారు. తానే అర్జునునితో పోరాడతానని అశ్వత్థామ ప్రతిజ్ఞ చేస్తాడు; భీకర సంహారం కొనసాగుతుంది.","ta":"தன் மாமன் கிருபரைக் கர்ணன் அவமதித்ததால் சினமுற்ற அஸ்வத்தாமன் வாளை உயர்த்தி அவனைக் கொல்லப் பாய, துரியோதனனும் கிருபரும் சமாதானப்படுத்துகின்றனர். தானே அர்ஜுனனுடன் போரிடுவதாக அஸ்வத்தாமன் சபதம் செய்ய, கொடிய அழிவு தொடர்கிறது.","ml":"തന്റെ അമ്മാവനായ കൃപരെ കർണ്ണൻ അപമാനിച്ചതിൽ കോപിച്ച അശ്വത്ഥാമാവ് അദ്ദേഹത്തെ കൊല്ലാൻ വാൾ ഉയർത്തുന്നു; ദുര്യോധനനും കൃപരും അവരെ ശാന്തരാക്കുന്നു. പിന്നീട് അശ്വത്ഥാമാവ് താൻ തന്നെ അർജുനനോട് പൊരുതുമെന്ന് പ്രതിജ്ഞയെടുക്കുന്നു; വലിയ കൂട്ടക്കൊലയോടെ യുദ്ധം തുടരുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.134; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"घटोत्कचवधपर्व","titleEn":"Ghatotkachavadha Parva (Slaying of Ghatotkacha)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तथा परुषितं दृष्ट्वा सूतपुत्रेण मातुलम् ।\nखड्गमुद्यम्य वेगेन द्रौणिरभ्यपतद्द्रुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing his uncle Kripa spoken to so harshly by the charioteer's son, Drona's son lifted his sword and rushed swiftly at Karna."}},{"text":"अश्वत्थामोवाच","meaning":{"en":"Ashvatthaman said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"कर्ण पश्य सुदुर्बुद्धे तिष्ठेदानीं नराधम ।\nएष तेऽद्य शिरः कायादुद्धरामि सुदुर्मते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Look, Karna, you fool! Stand where you are, you lowest of men. Today I will cut your head from your body, you wretch."}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"तमुत्पतन्तं वेगेन राजा दुर्योधनः स्वयम् ।\nन्यवारयन्महाराज कृपश्च द्विपदां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he sprang forward in fury, King Duryodhana himself held him back, O great king, and so did Kripa, best of men."}},{"text":"कर्ण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Karna said:"}},{"n":4,"text":"शूरोऽयं समरश्लाघी दुर्मतिश्च द्विजाधमः ।\nआसादयतु मद्वीर्यं मुञ्चेमं कुरुसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"This brahmin is brave but a boaster in battle and a fool, the lowest of the twice-born. Let him come and feel my strength. Let him go, best of the Kurus."}},{"text":"अश्वत्थामोवाच","meaning":{"en":"Ashvatthaman said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"तवैतत्क्षम्यतेऽस्माभिः सूतात्मज सुदुर्मते ।\nदर्पमुत्सिक्तमेतत्ते फल्गुनो नाशयिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"We forgive you this, you base-minded son of a charioteer. Arjuna will destroy this swollen pride of yours."}},{"text":"दुर्योधन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana said:"}},{"n":6,"text":"अश्वत्थामन्प्रसीदस्व क्षन्तुमर्हसि मानद ।\nकोपः खलु न कर्तव्यः सूतपुत्रे कथंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ashvatthaman, be calm; you who honor others should forgive. Anger must never be shown against the charioteer's son."}},{"n":7,"text":"त्वयि कर्णे कृपे द्रोणे मद्रराजेऽथ सौबले ।\nमहत्कार्यं समायत्तं प्रसीद द्विजसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"A great task rests on you, on Karna, Kripa, Drona, the king of Madra, and Shakuni's son. Be at peace, best of brahmins."}},{"n":8,"text":"एते ह्यभिमुखाः सर्वे राधेयेन युयुत्सवः ।\nआयान्ति पाण्डवा ब्रह्मन्नाह्वयन्तः समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Look, all these Pandavas are advancing from every side, eager to fight Karna and calling out challenges, O brahmin."}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":9,"text":"कर्णोऽपि रथिनां श्रेष्ठश्चापमुद्यम्य वीर्यवान् ।\nकौरवाग्र्यैः परिवृतः शक्रो देवगणैरिव ।\nपर्यतिष्ठत तेजस्वी स्वबाहुबलमाश्रितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna too, foremost of charioteers, mighty and radiant, raised his bow and stood relying on the strength of his own arms, surrounded by the chief Kauravas like Indra among the gods."}},{"n":10,"text":"ततः प्रववृते युद्धं कर्णस्य सह पाण्डवैः ।\nसंरब्धस्य महाराज सिंहनादविनादितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the battle of Karna with the Pandavas began, O great king, as he raged, and it echoed with lion-roars."}},{"n":11,"text":"ततस्ते पाण्डवा राजन्पाञ्चालाश्च यशस्विनः ।\nदृष्ट्वा कर्णं महाबाहुमुच्चैः शब्दमथानदन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Pandavas and the glorious Panchalas, O king, seeing mighty-armed Karna, shouted loudly."}},{"n":12,"text":"अयं कर्णः कुतः कर्णस्तिष्ठ कर्ण महारणे ।\nयुध्यस्व सहितोऽस्माभिर्दुरात्मन्पुरुषाधम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Here is Karna! Where can Karna go? Stand, Karna, in this great battle! Fight us, you wicked wretch, lowest of men!\""}},{"n":13,"text":"अन्ये तु दृष्ट्वा राधेयं क्रोधरक्तेक्षणाब्रुवन् ।\nहन्यतामयमुत्सिक्तः सूतपुत्रोऽल्पचेतनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Others, seeing Karna with eyes red with rage, said: \"Kill this arrogant, dull-witted charioteer's son!"}},{"n":14,"text":"सर्वैः पार्थिवशार्दूलैर्नानेनार्थोऽस्ति जीवता ।\nअत्यन्तवैरी पार्थानां सततं पापपूरुषः ॥","meaning":{"en":"None of these tigers among kings has any use for him alive; he is forever the bitter enemy of the Pandavas, a sinful man."}},{"n":15,"text":"एष मूलं ह्यनर्थानां दुर्योधनमते स्थितः ।\nहतैनमिति जल्पन्तः क्षत्रियाः समुपाद्रवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is the root of all these ills, firm in Duryodhana's counsel. Kill him!\" So the kshatriyas cried and rushed on him."}},{"n":16,"text":"महता शरवर्षेण छादयन्तो महारथाः ।\nवधार्थं सूतपुत्रस्य पाण्डवेयेन चोदिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Urged on by the Pandava, the great warriors covered the charioteer's son with a heavy rain of arrows, to kill him."}},{"n":17,"text":"तांस्तु सर्वांस्तथा दृष्ट्वा धावमानान्महारथान् ।\nन विव्यथे सूतपुत्रो न च त्रासमगच्छत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing all those great warriors rushing at him, the charioteer's son neither trembled nor felt fear."}},{"n":18,"text":"दृष्ट्वा नगरकल्पं तमुद्धूतं सैन्यसागरम् ।\nपिप्रीषुस्तव पुत्राणां संग्रामेष्वपराजितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Never beaten in battle, he looked at that army surging like a city-sized sea and, wishing to please your sons, he took action."}},{"n":19,"text":"सायकौघेन बलवान्क्षिप्रकारी महाबलः ।\nवारयामास तत्सैन्यं समन्ताद्भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Strong, quick-handed and very mighty, O best of Bharatas, he held back that army on every side with a flood of arrows."}},{"n":20,"text":"ततस्तु शरवर्षेण पार्थिवास्तमवारयन् ।\nधनूंषि ते विधुन्वानाः शतशोऽथ सहस्रशः ।\nअयोधयन्त राधेयं शक्रं दैत्यगणा इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the kings checked him with a rain of arrows, shaking their bows by the hundreds and thousands, and fought Karna as hosts of Daityas fought Indra."}},{"n":21,"text":"शरवर्षं तु तत्कर्णः पार्थिवैः समुदीरितम् ।\nशरवर्षेण महता समन्ताद्व्यकिरत्प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Karna, O lord, scattered all around, with a great rain of arrows, the rain of arrows loosed by the kings."}},{"n":22,"text":"तद्युद्धमभवत्तेषां कृतप्रतिकृतैषिणाम् ।\nयथा देवासुरे युद्धे शक्रस्य सह दानवैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Each side eager to repay the other, their battle was like the fight of Indra with the Danavas in the war of gods and demons."}},{"n":23,"text":"तत्राद्भुतमपश्याम सूतपुत्रस्य लाघवम् ।\nयदेनं समरे यत्ता नाप्नुवन्त परे युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"There we saw a marvel in the charioteer's son's swiftness: though the enemy strove in battle, they could not touch him."}},{"n":24,"text":"निवार्य च शरौघांस्तान्पार्थिवानां महारथः ।\nयुगेष्वीषासु छत्रेषु ध्वजेषु च हयेषु च ।\nआत्मनामाङ्कितान्बाणान्राधेयः प्राहिणोच्छितान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having turned aside those floods of royal arrows, the great warrior Karna sent sharp arrows marked with his own name into their yokes, shafts, umbrellas, banners and horses."}},{"n":25,"text":"ततस्ते व्याकुलीभूता राजानः कर्णपीडिताः ।\nबभ्रमुस्तत्र तत्रैव गावः शीतार्दिता इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the kings, tormented by Karna and thrown into confusion, wandered here and there like cows stricken with cold."}},{"n":26,"text":"हयानां वध्यमानानां गजानां रथिनां तथा ।\nतत्र तत्राभ्यवेक्षामः संघान्कर्णेन पातितान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here and there we saw groups of horses, elephants and charioteers struck down and slain by Karna."}},{"n":27,"text":"शिरोभिः पतितै राजन्बाहुभिश्च समन्ततः ।\nआस्तीर्णा वसुधा सर्वा शूराणामनिवर्तिनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fallen heads and arms lay everywhere, O king, and the whole earth was strewn with heroes who never turn back."}},{"n":28,"text":"हतैश्च हन्यमानैश्च निष्टनद्भिश्च सर्वशः ।\nबभूवायोधनं रौद्रं वैवस्वतपुरोपमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With the slain, the being-slain and the groaning all around, the battlefield became terrible, like the city of Yama."}},{"n":29,"text":"ततो दुर्योधनो राजा दृष्ट्वा कर्णस्य विक्रमम् ।\nअश्वत्थामानमासाद्य तदा वाक्यमुवाच ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Duryodhana, seeing Karna's prowess, went to Ashvatthaman and spoke these words."}},{"n":30,"text":"युध्यतेऽसौ रणे कर्णो दंशितः सर्वपार्थिवैः ।\nपश्यैतां द्रवतीं सेनां कर्णसायकपीडिताम् ।\nकार्त्तिकेयेन विध्वस्तामासुरीं पृतनामिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana said:"}},{"n":31,"text":"दृष्ट्वैतां निर्जितां सेनां रणे कर्णेन धीमता ।\nअभियात्येष बीभत्सुः सूतपुत्रजिघांसया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna is fighting in battle, armored, with all the kings; look at that army fleeing, tormented by Karna's arrows, like the host of asuras shattered by Kartikeya."}},{"n":32,"text":"तद्यथा पश्यमानानां सूतपुत्रं महारथम् ।\nन हन्यात्पाण्डवः संख्ये तथा नीतिर्विधीयताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing this army defeated in battle by the wise Karna, Arjuna is advancing here, wanting to kill the charioteer's son."}},{"n":33,"text":"ततो द्रौणिः कृपः शल्यो हार्दिक्यश्च महारथः ।\nप्रत्युद्ययुस्तदा पार्थं सूतपुत्रपरीप्सया ॥","meaning":{"en":"So take such measures that the Pandava cannot kill the great warrior Karna while we look on."}},{"n":34,"text":"आयान्तं दृश्य कौन्तेयं वृत्रं देवचमूमिव ।\nप्रत्युद्ययौ तदा कर्णो यथा शक्रः प्रतापवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Drona's son, Kripa, Shalya and the great warrior Hardikya (Kritavarman) went out to meet Partha, wishing to protect the charioteer's son."}},{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":35,"text":"संरब्धं फल्गुनं दृष्ट्वा कालान्तकयमोपमम् ।\nकर्णो वैकर्तनः सूत प्रत्यपद्यत्किमुत्तरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Arjuna in a rage, like Death, the ender of time, and Yama, what did Karna, son of Vikartana, do in answer, Sanjaya?"}},{"n":36,"text":"स ह्यस्पर्धत पार्थेन नित्यमेव महारथः ।\nआशंसते च बीभत्सुं युद्धे जेतुं सुदारुणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"That great warrior had always rivaled Partha, and hoped to defeat Bibhatsu in a most dreadful battle."}},{"n":37,"text":"स तु तं सहसा प्राप्तं नित्यमत्यन्तवैरिणम् ।\nकर्णो वैकर्तनः सूत किमुत्तरमपद्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"When his lifelong bitter enemy came upon him suddenly, what did Karna, Vikartana's son, do in reply, Sanjaya?"}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":38,"text":"आयान्तं पाण्डवं दृष्ट्वा गजः प्रतिगजं यथा ।\nअसंभ्रान्ततरः कर्णः प्रत्युदीयाद्धनंजयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the Pandava coming, Karna advanced to meet Dhananjaya, calmer than ever, as an elephant meets a rival elephant."}},{"n":39,"text":"तमापतन्तं वेगेन वैकर्तनमजिह्मगैः ।\nवारयामास तेजस्वी पाण्डवः शत्रुतापनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The radiant Pandava, tormentor of foes, checked Vikartana's son as he rushed on with speed, using straight-flying arrows."}},{"n":40,"text":"तं कर्णः शरजालेन छादयामास मारिष ।\nविव्याध च सुसंक्रुद्धः शरैस्त्रिभिरजिह्मगैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna covered him with a net of arrows, my lord, and in great anger pierced him with three straight arrows."}},{"n":41,"text":"तस्य तल्लाघवं पार्थो नामृष्यत महाबलः ।\nतस्मै बाणाञ्शिलाधौतान्प्रसन्नाग्रानजिह्मगान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mighty Partha could not bear his quickness. That tormentor of foes sent thirty whetstone-sharpened arrows with bright points and straight flight at the charioteer's son."}},{"n":42,"text":"प्राहिणोत्सूतपुत्राय त्रिंशतं शत्रुतापनः ।\nविव्याध चैनं संरब्धो बाणेनैकेन वीर्यवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Angry and powerful, he also pierced Karna with one arrow in the front of his left arm, as if laughing, with a nalika shaft. Struck by its force, the bow fell from Karna's hand."}},{"n":43,"text":"सव्ये भुजाग्रे बलवान्नाराचेन हसन्निव ।\nतस्य विद्धस्य वेगेन कराच्चापं पपात ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking up the bow again in half a moment, the mighty Karna covered Arjuna with floods of arrows, like a skilled expert."}},{"n":44,"text":"पुनरादाय तच्चापं निमेषार्धान्महाबलः ।\nछादयामास बाणौघैः फल्गुनं कृतहस्तवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhananjaya, smiling as it were, destroyed with his own rain of arrows that shower of arrows loosed by the charioteer's son, O Bharata."}},{"n":45,"text":"शरवृष्टिं तु तां मुक्तां सूतपुत्रेण भारत ।\nव्यधमच्छरवर्षेण स्मयन्निव धनंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Meeting each other, those two great archers, each eager to repay the other, covered one another with rains of arrows, O king."}},{"n":46,"text":"तौ परस्परमासाद्य शरवर्षेण पार्थिव ।\nछादयेतां महेष्वासौ कृतप्रतिकृतैषिणौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"That battle between Karna and the Pandava in the fight was wonderful, as of two enraged wild elephants fighting over a female."}},{"n":47,"text":"तदद्भुतमभूद्युद्धं कर्णपाण्डवयोर्मृधे ।\nक्रुद्धयोर्वाशिताहेतोर्वन्ययोर्गजयोरिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Partha, the great archer, seeing Karna's prowess, quickly cut his bow at the grip."}},{"n":48,"text":"ततः पार्थो महेष्वासो दृष्ट्वा कर्णस्य विक्रमम् ।\nमुष्टिदेशे धनुस्तस्य चिच्छेद त्वरयान्वितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The destroyer of foes sent his four horses to Yama's abode with broad-headed arrows and cut his charioteer's head from his body."}},{"n":49,"text":"अश्वांश्च चतुरो भल्लैरनयद्यमसादनम् ।\nसारथेश्च शिरः कायादहरच्छत्रुतापनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Partha, Pandu's joy, pierced him, bowless, horseless and without a charioteer, with four arrows."}},{"n":50,"text":"अथैनं छिन्नधन्वानं हताश्वं हतसारथिम् ।\nविव्याध सायकैः पार्थश्चतुर्भिः पाण्डुनन्दनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The bull among men, hurt by the arrows, quickly leapt down from his horseless chariot and mounted Kripa's chariot."}},{"n":51,"text":"हताश्वात्तु रथात्तूर्णमवप्लुत्य नरर्षभः ।\nआरुरोह रथं तूर्णं कृपस्य शरपीडितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Karna beaten, your troops, O best of Bharatas, driven by Dhananjaya's arrows, fled in all ten directions."}},{"n":52,"text":"राधेयं निर्जितं दृष्ट्वा तावका भरतर्षभ ।\nधनंजयशरैर्नुन्नाः प्राद्रवन्त दिशो दश ॥","meaning":{"en":"King Duryodhana, seeing them flee, turned them back and said these words."}},{"n":53,"text":"द्रवतस्तान्समालोक्य राजा दुर्योधनो नृप ।\nनिवर्तयामास तदा वाक्यं चेदमुवाच ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana said:"}},{"n":54,"text":"अलं द्रुतेन वः शूरास्तिष्ठध्वं क्षत्रियर्षभाः ।\nएष पार्थवधायाहं स्वयं गच्छामि संयुगे ।\nअहं पार्थान्हनिष्यामि सपाञ्चालान्ससोमकान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Enough of running, heroes! Stand firm, bulls among kshatriyas. I myself am going into the battle to kill Partha."}},{"n":55,"text":"अद्य मे युध्यमानस्य सह गाण्डीवधन्वना ।\nद्रक्ष्यन्ति विक्रमं पार्थाः कालस्येव युगक्षये ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will kill the Parthas with the Panchalas and Somakas. Today, as I fight the wielder of the Gandiva, the Parthas will see my prowess, like Time at the world's end."}},{"n":56,"text":"अद्य मद्बाणजालानि विमुक्तानि सहस्रशः ।\nद्रक्ष्यन्ति समरे योधाः शलभानामिवायतीः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Today the warriors will see thousands of my arrow-nets loosed in the battle, like flights of locusts."}},{"n":57,"text":"अद्य बाणमयं वर्षं सृजतो मम धन्विनः ।\nजीमूतस्येव घर्मान्ते द्रक्ष्यन्ति युधि सैनिकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Today, as I, the archer, send down a rain of arrows, the soldiers will see it in battle like a cloud at summer's end."}},{"n":58,"text":"जेष्याम्यद्य रणे पार्थं सायकैर्नतपर्वभिः ।\nतिष्ठध्वं समरे शूरा भयं त्यजत फल्गुनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Today I will conquer Partha in battle with arrows with bent joints. Stand, heroes; cast off your fear of Arjuna."}},{"n":59,"text":"न हि मद्वीर्यमासाद्य फल्गुनः प्रसहिष्यति ।\nयथा वेलां समासाद्य सागरो मकरालयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna cannot withstand my strength, as the ocean, home of sea monsters, cannot pass its shore."}},{"n":60,"text":"इत्युक्त्वा प्रययौ राजा सैन्येन महता वृतः ।\nफल्गुनं प्रति दुर्धर्षः क्रोधसंरक्तलोचनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, the invincible king, surrounded by a great army and his eyes red with fury, marched toward Arjuna."}},{"n":61,"text":"तं प्रयान्तं महाबाहुं दृष्ट्वा शारद्वतस्तदा ।\nअश्वत्थामानमासाद्य वाक्यमेतदुवाच ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the mighty-armed king go, Kripa, son of Sharadvat, went to Ashvatthaman and said this."}},{"n":62,"text":"एष राजा महाबाहुरमर्षी क्रोधमूर्छितः ।\nपतंगवृत्तिमास्थाय फल्गुनं योद्धुमिच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"This mighty-armed king, impatient and faint with rage, wants to fight Arjuna like a moth flying into a flame."}},{"n":63,"text":"यावन्नः पश्यमानानां प्राणान्पार्थेन संगतः ।\nन जह्यात्पुरुषव्याघ्रस्तावद्वारय कौरवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While we look on, bring back this Kuru king before the tiger among men meets Partha and loses his life."}},{"n":64,"text":"यावत्फल्गुनबाणानां गोचरं नाधिगच्छति ।\nकौरवः पार्थिवो वीरस्तावद्वारय तं द्रुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Quickly hold back the Kuru king, before he comes within range of Arjuna's arrows."}},{"n":65,"text":"यावत्पार्थशरैर्घोरैर्निर्मुक्तोरगसंनिभैः ।\nन भस्मीक्रियते राजा तावद्युद्धान्निवार्यताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Stop him from fighting before the king is turned to ash by Partha's dreadful arrows, which are like serpents just freed of their skins."}},{"n":66,"text":"अयुक्तमिव पश्यामि तिष्ठत्स्वस्मासु मानद ।\nस्वयं युद्धाय यद्राजा पार्थं यात्यसहायवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It seems to me improper, honored sir, that while we stand here the king himself goes to fight Partha without support."}},{"n":67,"text":"दुर्लभं जीवितं मन्ये कौरव्यस्य किरीटिना ।\nयुध्यमानस्य पार्थेन शार्दूलेनेव हस्तिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I think the Kuru king's life against Arjuna is hard to keep, as when a tiger fights an elephant, if he fights Partha."}},{"n":68,"text":"मातुलेनैवमुक्तस्तु द्रौणिः शस्त्रभृतां वरः ।\nदुर्योधनमिदं वाक्यं त्वरितं समभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Spoken to thus by his uncle, Drona's son, best of weapon-bearers, quickly said this to Duryodhana."}},{"n":69,"text":"मयि जीवति गान्धारे न युद्धं गन्तुमर्हसि ।\nमामनादृत्य कौरव्य तव नित्यं हितैषिणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While I live, son of Gandhari, you should not go to battle, ignoring me, who always wish you well, O Kuru."}},{"n":70,"text":"न हि ते संभ्रमः कार्यः पार्थस्य विजयं प्रति ।\nअहमावारयिष्यामि पार्थं तिष्ठ सुयोधन ॥","meaning":{"en":"You need not be anxious about Partha's victory. I will hold Partha back; stay, Suyodhana."}},{"text":"दुर्योधन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana said:"}},{"n":71,"text":"आचार्यः पाण्डुपुत्रान्वै पुत्रवत्परिरक्षति ।\nत्वमप्युपेक्षां कुरुषे तेषु नित्यं द्विजोत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"The teacher (Drona) protects the sons of Pandu like his own sons, and you too, best of brahmins, always treat them with indulgence."}},{"n":72,"text":"मम वा मन्दभाग्यत्वान्मन्दस्ते विक्रमो युधि ।\nधर्मराजप्रियार्थं वा द्रौपद्या वा न विद्म तत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Either because of my ill luck your prowess in battle is weak, or out of love for King Yudhishthira or Draupadi; I do not know which."}},{"n":73,"text":"धिगस्तु मम लुब्धस्य यत्कृते सर्वबान्धवाः ।\nसुखार्हाः परमं दुःखं प्राप्नुवन्त्यपराजिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shame on me, greedy as I am, because of whom all my kinsmen, who deserve happiness and were never defeated, suffer the greatest sorrow."}},{"n":74,"text":"को हि शस्त्रभृतां मुख्यो महेश्वरसमो युधि ।\nशत्रून्न क्षपयेच्छक्तो यो न स्याद्गौतमीसुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Who is the foremost of weapon-bearers, the equal of Maheshvara in battle, who could not destroy his enemies, if it were not the son of Gautami (Kripi)?"}},{"n":75,"text":"अश्वत्थामन्प्रसीदस्व नाशयैतान्ममाहितान् ।\nतवास्त्रगोचरे शक्ताः स्थातुं देवापि नानघ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ashvatthaman, be gracious and destroy these enemies of mine. Even gods, faultless one, cannot stand within range of your weapons."}},{"n":76,"text":"पाञ्चालान्सोमकांश्चैव जहि द्रौणे सहानुगान् ।\nवयं शेषान्हनिष्यामस्त्वयैव परिरक्षिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kill the Panchalas and the Somakas with their followers, son of Drona. Protected by you, we will kill the rest."}},{"n":77,"text":"एते हि सोमका विप्र पाञ्चालाश्च यशस्विनः ।\nमम सैन्येषु संरब्धा विचरन्ति दवाग्निवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"These Somakas, brahmin, and the glorious Panchalas, roam raging among my armies like a forest fire."}},{"n":78,"text":"तान्वारय महाबाहो केकयांश्च नरोत्तम ।\nपुरा कुर्वन्ति निःशेषं रक्ष्यमाणाः किरीटिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hold them back, mighty-armed best of men, and the Kekayas too, before, guarded by Kiritin (Arjuna), they leave nothing of us."}},{"n":79,"text":"आदौ वा यदि वा पश्चात्तवेदं कर्म मारिष ।\nत्वमुत्पन्नो महाबाहो पाञ्चालानां वधं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whether sooner or later, honored sir, this task is yours, mighty-armed one: you were born to kill the Panchalas."}},{"n":80,"text":"करिष्यसि जगत्सर्वमपाञ्चालं किलाच्युत ।\nएवं सिद्धाब्रुवन्वाचो भविष्यति च तत्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Unfailing one, you will make the whole world free of Panchalas. So the siddhas have spoken, and it will be so."}},{"n":81,"text":"न तेऽस्त्रगोचरे शक्ताः स्थातुं देवाः सवासवाः ।\nकिमु पार्थाः सपाञ्चालाः सत्यमेतद्वचो मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gods with Indra cannot stand within range of your weapons; how then the Parthas with the Panchalas? What I say is true."}}]}]}